                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Programs of study such as executive programs that are designed specifically to meet the needs of full-time members of the labour force" .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContribution> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                        rdfs:subClassOf :FinancialNeedAssessmentInputPattern ,
                                                                        <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "Expected Contribution" ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#ContributionFromAssets> ,
                                                                                                         <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#ParentsContribution> ,
                                                                                                         <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#ParentsContributionFromAssets> ,
                                                                                                         <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#StudentContributionFromIncome> ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A financial contribution from a student, parent, step-parent, sponsor, legal guardian or spouse to assist with the cost of the student’s program of study. The contribution is automatically assessed during the student need assessment process." ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00832> .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#ExpectedContributionFromNeedBasedBursaries> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "Expected Contribution from Need-Based Bursaries" ;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The expected contribution from need-based bursaries, where the eligibility criteria are based on need, but the funding is not targeted for a specific element of the costs of living or education. The expected contribution is equivalent to the assessed actual amount, less an exemption of $1,800 per program year for both merit-based scholarships and need-based bursaries combined. Any amount of scholarship/bursary funding above $1,800 is considered income and is assessed at 100%." .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FamilyIncome
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FamilyIncome> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                rdfs:subClassOf :FinancialNeedAssessmentInputPattern ,
                                                                <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                rdfs:label "Family Income" ;
                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#FamilySize> ,
                                                                                                 <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#IncomeAllowanceCalculation> ,
                                                                                                 <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/us#ParentsAvailableIncome> ;
                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "family income is defined as the student’s parent(s)/guardian(s)/sponsor(s) income (as reported on line 15000 [total income] of each parent(s)/guardian(s)/sponsor(s) previous year’s T1 General Income Tax and Benefit Return), or international equivalent." ,
                                                                                                 "family income is defined as the sum of student’s income and spouse’s/common-law partner’s income (as reported on both the student’s and spouse’s/common-law partner’s line 15000 [total income] of their respective previous year’s T1 General Income Tax and Benefit Return), or international equivalent." ;
                                                <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00410> ,
                                                                                           <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00411> .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FamilySize
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FamilySize> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                              rdfs:label "Family Size" ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Family size includes all children 18 years of age and under, all children aged 19 and over who are full-time dependent students, children with disabilities aged 19 and over, elderly relatives who are fully supported by the parent(s) and declared on the T1 General Income Tax and Benefit Return, and foster children where foster parent income is claimed on Appendix 1." ;
                                              <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00434> .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FederalFixedStudentContribution
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FederalFixedStudentContribution> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                   rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "Federal Fixed Student Contribution" ;
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The federal fixed student contribution, a calculated amount based on study weeks and capped at 34 2/3 weeks per loan year." ;
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00408> .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FieldPlacement
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FieldPlacement> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                  rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                  rdfs:label "Field Placement" ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A field placement provides students with an intensive part-time/short term intensive hands-on practical experience in a setting relevant to their subject of study. Field placements may not require supervision of a registered or licensed professional and the completed work experience hours are not required for professional certification. Field placements account for work-integrated educational experiences not encompassed by other forms, such as co-op, clinic, practicum, and internship." ;
                                                  <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://w3id.org/cco-gro/data#CAN_UNIT_00833> .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FieldTripPracticumClinicalPlacementFunding
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FieldTripPracticumClinicalPlacementFunding> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                              rdfs:subClassOf <https://www.w3id.org/cco/cco#Resource> ;
                                                                              rdfs:label "Field Trip and Placement Funding" ;
                                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Funding allocated for actual costs of field trips, practicums, and clinical placements that are essential elements of an educational program." .


###  https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FinancialAidOfficerRole
<https://w3id.org/cco-gro/onto/ca#FinancialAidOfficerRole> rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                           rdfs:subClassOf :FinancialAidAdministratorRolePattern ,
